// With you at the Mac (render/gel/face.h, showWithYou; render/gel/gaze.h), each on a frozen clock after a
// reset. Nothing told: it rests. Your pointer, while it moves: its eyes follow it and it leans and slides
// its way (to your left, your right, up), and at the screen's edge nearest it, it looks right at it and
// leans in. Scrolling: it reads along, a page beside it on the Mac's side, its lines scrolling up,
// turned and slid that way, lower, its eyes down on the page, travelling down a line and snapping back
// up with a nod; two minutes on, settled in, lids half down; with the screen above it, up at it. Typing
// fast: hunched in, eyes wide, paws quicker; a long stretch of typing stopped, a look up at you. Music:
// headphones on, half-closed eyes, a sway and notes rising, then a rest with the headphones still on,
// then a look round as it stops. A video: a small screen beside it, its light on the body, turned to it,
// taller, eyes wide, and a small start now and then. A call: still, smaller, eyes half, a muted mic by
// its ear; a stretch as it ends.
